{
  "name": "Siberys Powder (Keg)",
  "type": "consumable",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> Interact</p>\n<p>@Compendium[pathfinders-guide-to-eberron.eberron-items.jV0oBMJWcAPWvApn]{Siberys Powder (horn)}Siberys powder is a volatile and explosive alchemical substance commonly used in the production of wand munitions. Siberys powder becomes inert and useless when wet and must be kept in a sealed, water-tight container.</p>\n<p>A keg contains 5,000 doses of siberys powder and can be detonated in the same way as a @Compendium[pathfinders-guide-to-eberron.eberron-items.jV0oBMJWcAPWvApn]{Siberys powder (horn)}. As long as the keg is mostly full (at least 4,000 doses remaining) this deals [[/r 3d6[fire]]] damage in a @Template[type:burst|distance:20] (@Check[type:reflex|dc:20|basic:true|name:Siberys Powder Detonation] save). Detonating multiple kegs can increase the area, but not the damage, of this effect; detonating a keg and any horns at the same time in an overlapping area also doesn't increase the damage. </p>"
    },
